@format 1
@id keyframes.nearest
@title Move to nearest keyframe
@area 3. Keyframes and waveform
@entry input
@summary Compare the adjacent timestamps in the complete stored keyframe set and move immediately when either side has a candidate, without first confirming local scan coverage.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related keyframes.scan, keyframes.previous, keyframes.next

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias key = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LKeyframeOrchestrator

[input] Nearest-keyframe command <input>
- Dispatch the nearest-keyframe shortcut when timeline commands and a spool are active @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...)
> find

[find] Compare stored neighbours <decision>
- Resolve the strict previous and next timestamps from the entire stored keyframe set @ key.LKeyframeNearestMove(...)
- Choose the closer stored timestamp; an equal distance chooses the previous timestamp @ key.LKeyframeNearestMove(...)
- Make the choice without checking whether the span around the current cursor has been scanned @ key.LKeyframeNearestMove(...)
? "At least one stored neighbour exists" > move
? "No stored neighbour exists" > defer

[move] Move to stored candidate <process>
- Accept the non-null selected candidate and propagate it as the new cursor @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
- Update both timeline views, request a scan around the new position, and seek the preview @ flow.PFlowCursorPropagate(...)
> result

[result] Nearest stored keyframe selected <output>
= A remote stored keyframe can win even when no keyframe search has been performed around the requested cursor position.

[defer] Request scanning near current cursor <process>
- Defer a keyframe scan around the unchanged cursor only when neither stored neighbour exists @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
- Start the delayed scan request @ flow.PFlowKeyframeDefer(...)
> map:keyframes.scan
